  "verbalization": "Nepetoidin A is shown to have a target relationship with the CD276 antigen through multiple pathways, all of which converge on the MIP (Molecular Interaction Protein) as a common intermediate. The evidence suggests that Nepetoidin A interacts with MIP, which in turn is targeted by several compounds, including 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, Polygalasaponin XXXIII, and 9-Methoxy-4-(methoxymethyl)-3,5-dimethylbenzo[f][1]benzofuran. These compounds all share the same target, CD276 antigen, indicating a potential pathway where Nepetoidin A may modulate the activity of CD276 through these intermediates. The consistent scores across the three paths (0.4726, 0.4726, 0.4551) suggest a strong, albeit variable, level of confidence in the relationship. The mechanism likely involves Nepetoidin A interacting with MIP, which is a key player in the regulation of CD276, possibly through a common signaling or functional pathway. The evidence supports a plausible biological connection, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the role of MIP in this interaction.",
